From e352354b5d710625ba4196d041b0437e6d2ae3c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:30:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0211: the menu overlay. main_menu.c's code that only
 runs while a card menu is open is linked into MENU_REL.BIN at OVL_BTL_BASE,
 read where each opens (the title, the sleep save, the save machine, the
 game-clear save): 33 KB of every heap

loadMenuOverlay (runMainMenu, partner.c's sleep save, openSaveMachine, gameClearSave) reads it; closeMenuOverlay reads
KAR again on the curling screen (0x80053800, the same slot) when a menu closes in the world. The boot options
(modBootOptions, modCardOptions, modApplyOptions, isMemcardUnformatted), modNewGame, formatInteger, swapPartnerSpecies,
modReplayMainMenu and the entries stay in the executable, with all of the file's data, rodata and bss but the moved
functions' switch tables. config/us/overlay.ld names the moved functions one by one: a new function stays resident.
A VS battle from the title's registration screens reads VS_REL over the menu overlay: modMenuVsBattle (resident) runs
it and reads the menu overlay again before returning into tickMainMenu. MENU_REL.BIN is a new FILE_OFFSET_TABLE name;
a link ASSERT keeps its end below OVL_EVL_BASE (ENDI loads there during the game-clear save). xref.py check: the
executable's references into overlays are the series' plus these entries only. Heap at the tip 170 784 -> 203 824.
